        <categoryLink name="Morale" id="48fc-b5e6-4794-0017" hidden="false" targetId="2787-4749-a5bf-b2d7"/>
      </categoryLinks>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Composite Bows" id="5cbd-eeeb-54cc-97fc" hidden="false">
          <description>Magyar warriors don’t have access to bows, only composite bows. These have the same characteristics as bows, except that their range is 30”</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="The Bők" id="ed8d-8970-c85d-49af" hidden="false">
          <description>A Magyar chieftain is automatically a Bők.


A Bők can carry a spear, a sabre, a composite bow, a shield, and/or armour. Therefore, a Bők figure can choose which weapon from their arsenal to use at
the start of each combat.

Even once engaged, a Bők fighter can choose to change equipment during a fight, for example during a multiple combat.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Sabres" id="cc2d-df37-f370-1048" hidden="false">
          <description>Magyars don’t have hand weapons, they have sabres. A warrior equipped with a sabre has a -1 penalty to rolls to hit SA and FA enemy figures wearing armour.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="All Cavalry, All Archers" id="34d8-cc94-5dba-928b" hidden="false">
          <description>The 25% limit on shooters and cavalry don’t apply to the Magyars.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Poor Bloody Infantry" id="79aa-f351-3853-7dde" hidden="false">
          <description>Magyar infantry figures have a -1 penalty to all their defence rolls in melee.


Magyar infantry figures have a -1 penalty to all their morale checks. 


Magyar infantry figures all have a -1” movement penalty. This penalty stacks with other movement penalties like armour, difficult terrain, etc.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Mounted Archers" id="2336-b346-fcd8-7205" hidden="false">
          <description>Magyar cavalry figures can be equipped with composite bows. Cavalry use composite bows with the same rules and restrictions as if they were infantry.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </forceEntry>
